"To find the positive difference between \\(120\\%\\) of 30 and \\(130\\%\\) of 20, we first need to calculate each percentage separately.\n\n1. Calculate \\(120\\%\\) of 30:\n   \\[\n   120\\% \\text{ of } 30 = \\frac{120}{100} \\times 30 = 1.2 \\times 30 = 36\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(130\\%\\) of 20:\n   \\[\n   130\\% \\text{ of } 20 = \\frac{130}{100} \\times 20 = 1.3 \\times 20 = 26\n   \\]\n\n3. Find the positive difference between the two results:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Positive difference} = | 36 - 26| = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between \\(120\\%\\) of 30 and \\(130\\%\\) of 20 is \\(\\boxed{10}\\)."
"To solve the equation \\( |5x - 1| = |3x + 2| \\), we need to consider the properties of absolute values. The absolute value equation \\( |A| = |B| \\) implies that either \\( A = B \\) or \\( A = -B \\).\n\nFirst, we solve the equation \\( 5x - 1 = 3x + 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n5x - 1 = 3x + 2 \\implies 5x - 3x = 2 + 1 \\implies 2x = 3 \\implies x = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve the equation \\( 5x - 1 = -(3x + 2) \\):\n\n\\[\n5x - 1 = -3x - 2 \\implies 5x + 3x = -2 + 1 \\implies 8x = -1 \\implies x = -\\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nThe smallest value of \\( x \\) that satisfies \\( |5x - 1| = |3x + 2| \\) is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{8}}\\)."
