"The roots of the quadratic $4x^2 + 7x + k$ are given as $\\frac{-7 \\pm i\\sqrt{15}}{8}$. These roots are complex conjugates, and their sum and product can be found using Vieta's formulas.\n\nFirst, let's find the sum of the roots:\n\\[\n\\frac{-7 + i\\sqrt{15}}{8} + \\frac{-7 - i\\sqrt{15}}{8} = \\frac{-14}{8} = -\\frac{7}{4}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's find the product of the roots:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{-7 + i\\sqrt{15}}{8}\\right)\\left(\\frac{-7 - i\\sqrt{15}}{8}\\right) = \\frac{(-7)^2 - (i\\sqrt{15})^2}{8^2} = \\frac{49 + 15}{64} = \\frac{64}{64} = 1\n\\]\n\nThe product of the roots is also $k$, so:\n\\[\nk = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $\\boxed{1}$."
