"To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expression \\(9 \\& 2\\) using the given operation definition:\n\n\\[\na \\& b = \\frac{\\sqrt{ b + a}}{\\sqrt{ab - b}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, substitute \\(a = 9\\) and \\(b = 2\\) into the operation:\n\n\\[\n9 \\& 2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{9 \\cdot 2 + 9}}{\\sqrt{9 \\cdot 2 - 2}}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expressions inside the square roots:\n\n\\[\n9 \\cdot 2 + 9 = 18 + 9 = 27\n\\]\n\\[\n9 \\cdot 2 - 2 = 18 - 2 = 16\n\\]\n\nNow, take the square roots:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{27} = 3\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt{16} = 4\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these values back into the fraction:\n\n\\[\n9 \\& 2 = \\frac{3}{4}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(9 \\& 2\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{4}}\\)."
