"To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt{19+3y} = 7\\), we need to isolate \\(y\\). Let's go through the steps:\n\n1. **Square both sides of the equation to eliminate the square root:**\n   \\[\n   (\\sqrt{19+3y})^2 = 7^2\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   19 + 3y = 49\n   \\]\n\n2. **Isolate the term with \\(y\\) by subtracting 19 from both sides:**\n   \\[\n   19 + 3y - 19 = 49 - 19\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   3y = 30\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(y\\) by dividing both sides by 3:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3y}{3} = \\frac{30}{3}\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   y = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(y\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\)."
"Let \\( t \\) be the number of hours since Jane started growing Sphere. Since she started growing Rod five hours before Sphere, Rod has been growing for \\( t - 5 \\) hours.\n\nThe population of Rod doubles every hour, so the population of Rod after \\( t - 5 \\) hours is:\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 2^{(t-5)} \\]\n\nThe population of Sphere quadruples every hour, so the population of Sphere after \\( t \\) hours is:\n\\[ 8 \\cdot 4^t \\]\n\nAt 8 p.m., the populations are equal, so we set up the equation:\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 2^{(t-5)} = 8 \\cdot 4^t \\]\n\nWe can simplify this equation by dividing both sides by 2:\n\\[ 2^{(t-5)} = 4^t \\]\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\\[ t - 5 = 2t \\]\n\nSolving for \\( t \\):\n\\[ -5 = -t \\]\n\\[ t = 5 \\]\n\nTherefore, Jane started growing Sphere \\(\\boxed{5}\\) hours ago."
