"Let the first term of the arithmetic series be $a$ and the common difference be $d$.\n\nThe sum of the first 5 terms is given by:\n\\[ 5(a + 4d) = 70 \\]\n\nThe sum of the first 10 terms is given by:\n\\[ 10(a + 9d) = 210 \\]\n\nWe can simplify these equations:\n\\[ a + 4d = 14 \\]\n\\[ a + 9d = 21 \\]\n\nNow, we solve this system of linear equations. Subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[ (a + 9d) - (a + 4d) = 21 - 14 \\]\n\\[ 5d = 7 \\]\n\\[ d = 1 \\]\n\nSubstitute $d = 1$ back into the first equation:\n\\[ a + 4(1) = 14 \\]\n\\[ a + 4 = 14 \\]\n\\[ a = 10 \\]\n\nTherefore, the first term of the series is \\(\\boxed{10} \\)."
