"Let \\( r \\) be the number of rows in the auditorium, and \\( s \\) be the number of seats per row. The total number of seats in the auditorium is \\( r \\cdot s = 450 \\).\n\nIf there are three fewer seats per row, the new number of seats per row is \\( s - 3 \\). If there are five extra rows, the new number of rows is \\( r + 5 \\). The total number of seats in this new arrangement is \\( (r + 5) \\cdot (s - 3) = 450 \\).\n\nWe already know \\( r \\cdot s = 450 \\), so we can substitute this into the equation:\n\n\\[ (r + 5)(450/r - 3) = 450 \\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n\\[ 450 - 3r + 15 = 450 \\]\n\\[ -3r = -15 \\]\n\\[ r = 5 \\]\n\nTherefore, the auditorium has 5 rows.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $5$. I hope it is correct."
