"We start with the given equations:\n\\[\n(x + y)^2 + (x - y)^2 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n(x + y)^4 + (x - y)^4 = 98\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the first equation:\n\\[\n(x + y)^2 + (x - y)^2 = 2x^2 + 2y^2 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 5\n\\]\n\nNext, let's simplify the second equation:\n\\[\n(x + y)^4 + (x - y)^4 = 2(x^2 + y^2)^2 - 2xy^2 = 98\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^2 - 2xy^2 = 98\n\\]\n\\[\n50 - 2xy^2 = 98\n\\]\n\\[\n-2xy^2 = 48\n\\]\n\\[\nxy^2 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\nxy = \\sqrt{24}\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\(xy\\) is \\(\\boxed{sqrt{24}}\\)."
