"To determine the number of distinct arrangements of the word \"PAPA,\" we need to consider the permutations of the letters. The word \"PAPA\" consists of 4 letters, where the letter \"P\" appears 3 times.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of permutations if all letters were distinct. Since there are 4 letters, the total number of permutations is:\n\n\\[\n4! = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24\n\\]\n\nHowever, since the letter \"P\" appears 3 times, we need to adjust for the repetition. We do this by dividing by the factorial of the number of times \"P\" appears, which is \\(3!\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4!}{3!}\n\\]\nwhere \n\n\\[\n3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of distinct arrangements of the letters in \"PAPA\" is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24}{6} = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of distinct arrangements of the word \"PAPA\" is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]"
