"First, we need to determine the total number of ways to choose 3 cards from a deck of 52 cards. This can be calculated using the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{52}{3} = \\frac{52!}{3!(52-3)!} = \\frac{52 \\times 51 \\times 50}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 22100\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the number of ways to choose 3 hearts from the 13 hearts in the deck. This is simply the number of ways to choose 3 items from 13:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{13}{3} = \\frac{13!}{3!(13-3)!} = 286\n\\]\n\nThe probability that all three cards dealt are hearts is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of possible outcomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{286}{22100} = \\frac{1}{80}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the probability is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{80}}"
