"To determine whether the function \\( f(x) = 7x^7 - 4x^4 + 1 \\) is even, odd, or neither, we need to test the symmetry properties of the function.\n\nA function \\( f(x) \\) is even if \\( f(-x) = f(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in the domain of \\( f \\).\nA function \\( f(x) \\) is odd if \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in the domain of \\( f \\).\n\nLet's compute \\( f(-x) \\):\n\n\\[\nf(-x) = 7(-x)^7 - 4(-x)^4 + 1\n\\]\n\nSince \\((-x)^7 = -x^7\\) and \\((-x)^4 = x^4\\), we have:\n\n\\[\nf(-x) = 7(-x^7) - 4x^4 + 1 = -7x^7 - 4x^4 + 1\n\\]\n\nSince \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\), the function \\( f(x) \\) is \\boxed{\\text{odd}}."
