"To solve the expression \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2} \\frac{2}{3}\\), we will break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, simplify the exponentiation:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2} = \\frac{2^2}{3^2} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply this result by \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{4}{9} = \\frac{2 \\cdot 4}{3 \\cdot 9} = \\frac{8}{27}\n\\]\n\nFinally, multiply this result by \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{8}{27} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{8 \\cdot 2}{27 \\cdot 3} = \\frac{16}{81} = \\frac{8}{27} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{9}}\\). I hope it is correct."
