"To determine the height of the hot air balloon after 25 more seconds, we need to calculate the total increase in height over that period and then add it to the initial height.\n\n1. **Calculate the total increase in height:**\n   The balloon is rising at a constant rate of 2 feet per second. Therefore, the total increase in height over 25 seconds is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total increase in height} = \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time} = 2 \\text{ feet/second} \\times 25 \\text{ seconds} = 50 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the final height:**\n   The initial height of the balloon is 10 feet. Adding the total increase in height gives:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Final height} = \\text{Initial height} + \\text{Total increase in height} = 10 \\text{ feet} + 50 \\text{ feet} = 60 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the height of the balloon after 25 more seconds is \\(\\boxed{60}\\) feet."
