"To find the area of triangle \\(ABC\\), we need to determine the lengths of its sides and the height.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(BD = 3\\)\n- \\(DC = 2 \\times BD = 2 \\times 3 = 6\\)\n- \\(BC = BD + DC = 3 + 6 = 9\\)\n\nThe height of triangle \\(ABC\\) from \\(A\\) to \\(BC\\) is given as 4 units.\n\nThe area \\(A\\) of a triangle is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} \\]\n\nHere, the base is \\(BC = 9\\) and the height is 4 units.\n\nSo, the area of triangle \\(ABC\\) is:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 9 \\times 4 \\]\n\\[ A = 9 \\times 2 \\]\n\\[ A = 18 \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\boxed{18}.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $18$. I hope it is correct."
