"To find the height \\( h \\) of \\(\\triangle PQR\\), we start with the formula for the area of a triangle:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- The area of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is \\(27 \\, \\text{cm}^2\\).\n- The base of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is \\(6 \\, \\text{cm}\\).\n\nLet \\( h \\) be the height of \\(\\triangle PQR\\). Substituting the given values into the area formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n27 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times h\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n27 = 3h\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( h \\), divide both sides of the equation by 3:\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{27}{3} = 9\n\\]\n\nThus, the height \\( h \\) of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is 9 cm.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $9$. I hope it is correct."
