"Let the five consecutive integers be \\( x, x+1, x+2, x+3, \\) and \\( x+4 \\).\n\nThe mean (average) of these five integers is given as 21. Therefore, we can write the equation for the mean as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x + (x+1) + (x+2) + (x+3) + (x+4)}{5} = 21\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5x + 10}{5} = 21\n\\]\n\nMultiply both sides by 5 to clear the fraction:\n\n\\[\n5x + 10 = 105\n\\]\n\nSubtract 10 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n5x = 95\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 5:\n\n\\[\nx = 19\n\\]\n\nThus, the five consecutive integers are \\( 19, 20,21, 22, 23 \\). The smallest of these integers is 19.\n\nTherefore, the smallest of the five integers is \\(\\boxed{19}\\)."
