"We start by expressing the coordinates \\((x, y)\\) in terms of \\(t\\):\n\\[\nx = t + \\frac{1}{t}\n\\]\n\\[\ny = t - \\frac{1}{t}\n\\]\n\nNext, we square the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n\\[\nx^2 = \\left( t + \\frac{1}{t} \\right)^2 = t^2 + 2 + \\frac{1}{t^2}\n\\]\n\\[\ny^2 = \\left( t - \\frac{1}{t} \\right)^2 = t^2 - 2 + \\frac{1}{t^2}\n\\]\n\nAdding these two equations, we get:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = (t^2 + 2 + \\frac{1}{t^2}) + (t^2 - 2 + \\frac{1}{t^2}) = 4\n\\]\n\nThis equation represents the equation of a circle with center at at \\((0, 0)\\) and radius 2. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\)."
