"First, we simplify the angles inside the sine functions:\n\n\\[1998^\\circ + 237^\\circ = 2235^\\circ\\]\n\\[1998^\\circ - 1653^\\circ = 345^\\circ\\]\n\nNext, we reduce these angles modulo \\(360^\\circ\\) to bring them within the standard range of \\(0^\\circ\\) to \\(360^\\circ\\):\n\n\\[2235^\\circ \\mod 360^\\circ = 235^\\circ\\]\n\\[345^\\circ \\mod 360^\\circ = 45^\\circ\\]\n\nNow, we evaluate the sine of these angles:\n\n\\[\\sin(235^\\circ) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\n\\[\\sin(45^\\circ) = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\n\nFinally, we multiply these values together:\n\n\\[\\left(-\\frac{{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) = -1\\]\n\nThus, the value is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\)."
