"The projection of $\\bold{v}$ onto $\\bold{w}$ is given by the formula:\n\n$$\\text{proj}_{\\bold{w}} \\bold{v} = \\frac{\\bold{v} \\cdot \\bold{w}}{\\bold{w} \\cdot \\bold{w}} \\bold{w}.$$\n\nFirst, we compute the dot products:\n\n$$\\bold{v} \\cdot \\bold{w} = (0)(2) + (-4)(2) + (1)(-1) = -9,$$\n\n$$\\bold{w} \\cdot \\bold{w} = (2)(2) + (2)(2) + (-1)(-1) = 4 + 4 + 1 = 9.$$\n\nNow, we substitute these values into the formula:\n\n$$\\text{proj}_{\\bold{w}} \\bold{v} = \\frac{-9}{9} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of $\\bold{v}$ onto $\\bold{w}$ is:\n\n$$\\boxedboxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}}.$$"
